[2.0, "o", "\u001b[2m04:03\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m\u270e note\u001b[0m \u001b[32mShort-shipped bags are now coming in a wave: LS328 at NCL (65), LS223 and LS236 at LBA (58 and 51). All rushed. The pattern is slotted departures pushing back the moment the CTOT window opens and leaving the last trolley behind. Rushing costs a BUM message and some ramp effort; holding costs close to a million each and a bad night for a plane-load of holidaymakers.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
